{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Convert all AddXXX and UpdateXXX functions to SetXXX, changing behavior to replace existing values. For map-based config values, directly overwrite. For slice-based values like AnchorPeer, implement duplicate detection by comparing struct fields (host/port) and replace existing entry instead of appending.",
    "U2: Rename Base() to BaseConfig() and Updated() to UpdatedConfig() for clarity. Update all references and GoDoc accordingly.",
    "U3: Introduce intermediate wrapper types (Application, Organization, Orderer, Consortium) that wrap ConfigGroup protos. ConfigTx will expose methods like Application(), Orderer(), Consortium() returning these wrappers. Wrappers will contain getter/setter methods for their respective config values, enabling chaining (e.g., c.Application().Org(orgName).SetAnchorPeer()). Existing flat functions on ConfigTx will be deprecated but kept for backward compatibility.",
    "U4: Create new 'orderer' subpackage under configtx. Move types: Orderer, BatchSize, Kafka, EtcdRaft, ConsensusState. Keep Policies as map[string]*cb.Policy in configtx due to shared policy functions. Update all imports and references.",
    "U5: Create new 'membership' subpackage under configtx. Move types: MSP, SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs. Update all imports and references.",
    "U6: Modify all RemoveXXX functions to return nil error when target value doesn't exist. Remove error return entirely for functions that cannot fail otherwise (only nil config check). Update GoDoc to explicitly state 'no error if value not present'.",
    "U7: Follow GoDoc best practices: improve New() documentation, remove 8 specified trivial examples, rename Example_XXX functions to descriptive names (Example_SystemChannelGenesis, Example_ApplicationChannelCreation, Example_ConfigUpdate, Example_PolicyRetrieval, Example_OrdererUpdate, Example_Membership), add focused examples for key workflows, remove output validation from examples, format code blocks with line breaks to prevent horizontal scrolling.",
    "U8: Implement CLI using Cobra framework. Structure: configtx [genesis|channel|update] with subcommands and flags. Genesis: system channel genesis block. Channel: application channel creation transaction. Update: config update transactions with subcommands for each updatable property (addAnchorPeer, setBatchSize, etc.). CLI will be placed in cmd/configtxcli. Integrate with existing configtx library functions."
  ],
